[{:db/id "q-61705/selection/0a37501bd5a3cdbd35a0c3bacde7f1d7749ed1190c8ade56bc3451d31c0f5e00" :answer/id #uuid "534c30cd-fb91-5d73-a130-bbcbb6b18e26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61705/selection/95634a9e8b40232c50421671ec0cda4a8e6c20a462cca7569b7cfb1e8ceadf85" :answer/id #uuid "d2911c93-110c-5b4a-bbd6-1bf9a421d5a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "142\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61705/selection/e0705e7eb5099dc6f14725733a9ddb703848d21269125121a98071373b9cb557" :answer/id #uuid "f1828f98-4786-5226-a063-0b73d2757f28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61705/selection/1dae3aef9ab0a3f92babd26aa95e99f1ef45418c2ba211b208d80336a769c897" :answer/id #uuid "1a4b29d0-df4c-5668-bfcf-e3143e442641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "116\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61705/selection/723dc4627d62ee2b0b160b607ba567f4db968d98f8e35566b1525aef0c9e7deb" :answer/id #uuid "80a20c95-701b-5f59-894b-467ccfcb4639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "126\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61705/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a431bdc3-b162-55af-82be-915961c75955" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-61705/selection/0a37501bd5a3cdbd35a0c3bacde7f1d7749ed1190c8ade56bc3451d31c0f5e00" :answer-field/choices ["q-61705/selection/0a37501bd5a3cdbd35a0c3bacde7f1d7749ed1190c8ade56bc3451d31c0f5e00" "q-61705/selection/95634a9e8b40232c50421671ec0cda4a8e6c20a462cca7569b7cfb1e8ceadf85" "q-61705/selection/e0705e7eb5099dc6f14725733a9ddb703848d21269125121a98071373b9cb557" "q-61705/selection/1dae3aef9ab0a3f92babd26aa95e99f1ef45418c2ba211b208d80336a769c897" "q-61705/selection/723dc4627d62ee2b0b160b607ba567f4db968d98f8e35566b1525aef0c9e7deb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-61705" :question/id #uuid "2a7cfcf9-d573-54e4-af00-b3e2f3d9834c" :question/math-academy-id "q-61705" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/4b0c67b6a8c18b4f05198c209dae8cb960c9bfdcfc8310d0f59ee7a717e68f41.png)\n\nAssuming that all side faces have the same height of $8\\,\\text{cm}$, find the total surface area of the square pyramid above using its net." :question/worked-solution "The net of our pyramid is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/1fc39646f2b26116f97bc5340b0a7211911ba64ae59e4ce652bf13018fb7ef33.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with a side equal to $6\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=6\\times 6=36\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $6\\,\\text{cm}$ and the height is $8\\,\\text{cm}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 6\\times 8=24\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =(\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =36+4\\times 24 \\\\  & =36+96 \\\\  & =132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-61705/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-61705"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-61907/selection/45df6082e3095b09e4ba5467ec9c3688495881b87a1f8ce56d93270704eced3a" :answer/id #uuid "31e13b82-dfc0-5253-a9e0-683206ae8f15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "175\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61907/selection/6915cc4ebd1a3d0cc243c76f0ae92ce93285886dfbda39afac2285fdc89e3b20" :answer/id #uuid "0c54a474-6a7e-5848-8a57-b229ac9c8c09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "200\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61907/selection/96c26fbc4e993d194ead915e322240f7526828f21d9dc4559e23291274fdbeb1" :answer/id #uuid "974098d5-4a74-5bc6-8e9f-176b542a656c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61907/selection/292e85c39a668615b2aec1bcfcc4880856e384b78806ace2256fcec0cbc2f1f5" :answer/id #uuid "2fb08f65-bdfb-5d0d-8d51-6bcf5c70d142" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "125\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61907/selection/9b58ee459d5d693318022f505ee0bb1c468611049145fe5c561e7d32b3601194" :answer/id #uuid "cac128f3-1f0f-51cc-a295-f0cf0466b10b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-61907/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b655c15c-1eba-55c7-93bf-48858a513d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-61907/selection/96c26fbc4e993d194ead915e322240f7526828f21d9dc4559e23291274fdbeb1" :answer-field/choices ["q-61907/selection/45df6082e3095b09e4ba5467ec9c3688495881b87a1f8ce56d93270704eced3a" "q-61907/selection/6915cc4ebd1a3d0cc243c76f0ae92ce93285886dfbda39afac2285fdc89e3b20" "q-61907/selection/96c26fbc4e993d194ead915e322240f7526828f21d9dc4559e23291274fdbeb1" "q-61907/selection/292e85c39a668615b2aec1bcfcc4880856e384b78806ace2256fcec0cbc2f1f5" "q-61907/selection/9b58ee459d5d693318022f505ee0bb1c468611049145fe5c561e7d32b3601194"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-61907" :question/id #uuid "e80ccdcb-f8a7-5672-8914-73b42c8ccce6" :question/math-academy-id "q-61907" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/d480892817efecf5ebea6860bece7cbae8127a9840e94ece34f9e83313abd5e5.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the cube above if it is $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/efca24e18b188363ec3698ff4deaa5d5bd4ec1bdb5075138f925573a407c1f79.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares only.\n\nThe squares are $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=5\\times 5=25\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the cube consists of $6$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =6\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =6\\times 25 \\\\  & =150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-61907/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-61907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93262/selection/5e8cd4eadf86d9352ac054bfe7f0912baceb36e3c05b2a91cb9f47e2a0c5c5c4" :answer/id #uuid "dfda0720-c887-56dd-be2c-4c40041ae20f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "370\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93262/selection/475139e9509a465b799b41230dd4bed95be09e18d0e9bbcd5171c710dec969ec" :answer/id #uuid "150d41e1-88e6-597c-9822-f7baadc67066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "390\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93262/selection/f6f387f6ac06ba1f4029ac43ef5a9df5b7c55fdb1d4d77747d554727336a65f6" :answer/id #uuid "95335036-0d3e-5ad6-9464-d14b33b0cb99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "450\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93262/selection/f2438397bc38b7a03e8c37304880f0a4043156a6e43c81e6f4c1aedf2b680f90" :answer/id #uuid "f96e2017-5817-59ea-8405-c52c86f24ef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "480\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93262/selection/5c8f9675a112317a0b79426ddf3124c0bd753781dbe4237eb553dd855d3b7e4e" :answer/id #uuid "254e4b31-ec04-5d7e-98c8-a193dbf60d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "470\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93262/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5778cc83-438b-5adb-a053-a68a0b7e7e14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93262/selection/5c8f9675a112317a0b79426ddf3124c0bd753781dbe4237eb553dd855d3b7e4e" :answer-field/choices ["q-93262/selection/5e8cd4eadf86d9352ac054bfe7f0912baceb36e3c05b2a91cb9f47e2a0c5c5c4" "q-93262/selection/475139e9509a465b799b41230dd4bed95be09e18d0e9bbcd5171c710dec969ec" "q-93262/selection/f6f387f6ac06ba1f4029ac43ef5a9df5b7c55fdb1d4d77747d554727336a65f6" "q-93262/selection/f2438397bc38b7a03e8c37304880f0a4043156a6e43c81e6f4c1aedf2b680f90" "q-93262/selection/5c8f9675a112317a0b79426ddf3124c0bd753781dbe4237eb553dd855d3b7e4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93262" :question/id #uuid "874f7685-d103-5726-ba3b-57ef24e4bac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93262" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/d2fe4346f503215ec6594655cf633ad46b62bc87572339bd1728e6535bef851a.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular pyramid represented by the net above?" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 150+4\\times 80 \\\\  & =150+320 \\\\  & =470\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93262/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a19512-4ba7-59c1-ae00-7b8f158264fe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93262"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93343/selection/a78ee97101cc1792169e4c771f6677c62fcd059b86e266391248eb0140defc8b" :answer/id #uuid "964a496d-5548-5d20-ad43-26cb2b140e66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93343/selection/9c8e5a985307c0380c82b845424311b3f55c05ea8ac25dbe539081353962c8a8" :answer/id #uuid "dec571db-d2ae-5656-99b9-c8bb6f0de6da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93343/selection/1864e6d3ca1a25f8c3c69350879a6bd4b94240e0a6691d58968334b9babb5a5a" :answer/id #uuid "b91af242-7352-528f-8aa4-1c8b71c3a55f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93343/selection/9d8aa2f5495c4ede6f0c335a2ebb89462c80a47072c3eddd213fdee5f97eecac" :answer/id #uuid "eab26e7c-e3c8-5894-9f41-fd9c42d0a241" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93343/selection/2c2bca1997ac8423478110765ead180821d1724e7b738a7278bb2827be16a324" :answer/id #uuid "f422fbea-9765-532b-b9ca-c6f898e45522" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "46\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93343/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c555f5-b80c-5954-aed6-442177da0a71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93343/selection/9d8aa2f5495c4ede6f0c335a2ebb89462c80a47072c3eddd213fdee5f97eecac" :answer-field/choices ["q-93343/selection/a78ee97101cc1792169e4c771f6677c62fcd059b86e266391248eb0140defc8b" "q-93343/selection/9c8e5a985307c0380c82b845424311b3f55c05ea8ac25dbe539081353962c8a8" "q-93343/selection/1864e6d3ca1a25f8c3c69350879a6bd4b94240e0a6691d58968334b9babb5a5a" "q-93343/selection/9d8aa2f5495c4ede6f0c335a2ebb89462c80a47072c3eddd213fdee5f97eecac" "q-93343/selection/2c2bca1997ac8423478110765ead180821d1724e7b738a7278bb2827be16a324"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93343" :question/id #uuid "d119284d-a155-58d7-994e-d134bc9c1879" :question/math-academy-id "q-93343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/3d0b6b63883b58ecce92e395380b140b32946a4bb037e1829544539749412af9.png)\n\nLiz deconstructs a lantern and gets the net shown above. In the figure, the areas of two of its faces are shown. What is the total surface area of the lantern?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ triangle (base) and $3$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 5+3\\times 13 \\\\  & =5+39 \\\\  & =44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93343/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93343"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93345/selection/ac8475412b1bd4624ca20182ae07d812934939b5cdf501efbb7d2c1d04f4552a" :answer/id #uuid "dfbb9ed0-fffb-5a91-969a-38395037cd0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93345/selection/eac7ea0e089930890f526b43b1f29090649356184667263aefaa4c4ecfb5f853" :answer/id #uuid "1cee7620-a974-54bd-b464-183c697c6975" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93345/selection/7580e02261ed380739461c29939a2c1599f8f355d8655725d09b653b42027fba" :answer/id #uuid "773c57b3-945f-5976-9a82-2df9e373e851" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93345/selection/8d170996267e136308ed81eac7c83e38b62c2a3c4d2a4f522aee22ab45203477" :answer/id #uuid "2c3fb9d3-3252-57c9-affa-295244d45666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "59\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93345/selection/91c92104501ff03dc42672e71af642cf70ba327687bd68341f682ffaf2487ca7" :answer/id #uuid "82af3bb2-3827-5c22-8fcf-ff8b92facb75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93345/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65244b1e-c4ce-5466-8884-bbcf56568e37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93345/selection/7580e02261ed380739461c29939a2c1599f8f355d8655725d09b653b42027fba" :answer-field/choices ["q-93345/selection/ac8475412b1bd4624ca20182ae07d812934939b5cdf501efbb7d2c1d04f4552a" "q-93345/selection/eac7ea0e089930890f526b43b1f29090649356184667263aefaa4c4ecfb5f853" "q-93345/selection/7580e02261ed380739461c29939a2c1599f8f355d8655725d09b653b42027fba" "q-93345/selection/8d170996267e136308ed81eac7c83e38b62c2a3c4d2a4f522aee22ab45203477" "q-93345/selection/91c92104501ff03dc42672e71af642cf70ba327687bd68341f682ffaf2487ca7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93345" :question/id #uuid "bcc3ddc4-ae0f-5ef4-a719-c3482960a177" :question/math-academy-id "q-93345" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/a8264c635006c74c2d9a7ca4eb3ab8d937ae7b270b4567373d022186c787bbc1.png)\n\nAn artist makes a glass sculpture. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the sculpture. What is the total surface area of the sculpture?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & =2\\times 8+3\\times 17 \\\\  & =16+51 \\\\  & =67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93345/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93345"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
